  "title": "Duas for Each Hour of the Day",
  "data": "The day is divided into twelve hours, each dedicated to one of the Twelve Imams (a.s.) with a supplication of tawassul addressed to the Imam of that hour:\n[Dua for the First Hour](E67)\n[Dua for the Second Hour](E68)\n[Dua for the Third Hour](E69)\n[Dua for the Fourth Hour](E70)\n[Dua for the Fifth Hour](E71)\n[Dua for the Sixth Hour](E72)\n[Dua for the Seventh Hour](E73)\n[Dua for the Eighth Hour](E74)\n[Dua for the Ninth Hour](E75)\n[Dua for the Tenth Hour](E76)\n[Dua for the Eleventh Hour](E77)\n[Dua for the Twelfth Hour](E78)",
  "merits": "Shaykh al-Tusi, Sayyid Ibn Baqi, and Shaykh al-Kaf'ami have divided the day into twelve hours, dedicating each hour to one of the Twelve Imams and mentioning an advocacy-seeking supplication (tawassul) addressed to the Imam of that hour. Although these master scholars have not mentioned any tradition reported from the Holy Imams about this division, relying on the high regard of these scholars, it may be said that they would never say or do anything unless they had acquainted themselves with a narration indicating that saying or deed. The supplicatory prayers mentioned here are those quoted from Misbah al-Mutahajjid by Shaykh al-Tusi."
}
